            <ArticleTitle>Pseudoaneurysm--a treatable form of cardiac rupture.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudoaneurysm is an unusual complication of myocardial infarction. Although its pathogenesis is known, the course of the condition is obscure. The diagnosis is usually made post-mortally. We present a case of a pseudoaneurysm following a myocardial infarction, diagnosed at a routine polyclinical echocardiographic examination in a patient who at the time of diagnosis was free of symptoms. The patient was successfully operated upon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
